{
  "$schema": "../../schema/app.schema.json",
  "id": "cinema-studio",
  "name": "Cinema Studio",
  "section": "image",
  "pack": "image-flux3",
  "status": "ready",
  "higgsfield_feature": "Cinematic Cameras",
  "summary": "Pick genre, era, camera body, lens, focal length, aperture, lighting and color palette; they become part of the prompt.",
  "workflow": "workflow.api.json",
  "source": {
    "template": "image_flux3_klein_distilled_t2i.json",
    "comfyui": "0.42.0",
    "notes": "Camera and lens vocabulary from open-higgsfield-ai (MIT), src/lib/promptUtils.js. Camera, lens and focal options write the look they give, not the gear: with \"shot on a <camera>\" Z-Image drew the camera into the picture (run 20261020-133620-l40s), and \"no camera in the frame\" did not stop it (run 20261024-172353-h100). Since 25 Oct the still is drawn by FLUX 3 Image Klein (16:9, 1344x768) instead of Z-Image Turbo, without the prompt upsampler: the app writes the whole prompt. Since 26 Oct genre, era, lighting and color palette are selects too (Higgsfield's Cinema Studio 4.0 has film settings, lighting setups and palettes), and aspect ratio and resolution come from create-image's latent and its LatentUpscaleBy node."
  },
